# What must never be uploaded to a CLI deploy.
#
# Vercel installs dependencies and builds on its own machines, so shipping any
# of this is at best wasted bandwidth. Without this file the upload exceeded
# the 100 MB per-file limit on node_modules' SWC binaries and on the webpack
# cache under .next-build.
#
# .gitignore already covers most of it for git-based deploys; a CLI deploy
# uploads the working directory, which is why it needs saying again here.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output, including the separate directory used to verify a build while
# a dev server is running (NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next-build).
.next
**/.next
.next-build
**/.next-build

# Local environment files. Production configuration lives in Vercel's own
# environment variables; a .env reaching the build would be both wrong and a
# secret leak.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Local tooling, caches and test artefacts.
.git
.playwright-cli
coverage
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
